    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "@id": "https://www.lecremedelacrumb.com/air-fryer-chicken-breasts/#faq-question-1686947797793",
     "position": 1,
     "url": "https://www.lecremedelacrumb.com/air-fryer-chicken-breasts/#faq-question-1686947797793",
     "name": "How do I know if the chicken is cooked through?",
     "answerCount": 1,
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Especially when looking at breaded chicken, it might be difficult to know if the chicken is cooked through. I highly recommend using a meat thermometer so that you can check the internal temperature. I like to take chicken breast out of the air fryer once it has hit 155-160 F and then it continues cooking a bit further while it rests before serving. ",
      "inLanguage": "en-US"
     },
     "inLanguage": "en-US"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "@id": "https://www.lecremedelacrumb.com/air-fryer-chicken-breasts/#faq-question-1686948366270",
     "position": 2,
     "url": "https://www.lecremedelacrumb.com/air-fryer-chicken-breasts/#faq-question-1686948366270",
     "name": "How long to cook thin chicken breast in the air fryer?",
     "answerCount": 1,
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "If you cut the chicken into thinner pieces like I recommend doing with breaded chicken, the chicken will cook more quickly in the air fryer. However, the cooking time varies depending on the thickness of the chicken! I recommend cooking for 15 minutes and then checking the internal temperature of the chicken to determine if it needs any longer. ",
      "inLanguage": "en-US"
     },
     "inLanguage": "en-US"
